.SH NAME
maknoon-identity-publish - Publish your identity to a registry (WKD, DNS, or local)


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBmaknoon identity publish [handle] [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Publishes your identity (ML-KEM + ML-DSA public keys) to one or more registries
so that other Maknoon users can encrypt directly to you by handle.

.PP
Registries:
  --wkd       Web Key Directory — place a signed JSON file on your HTTPS server at
              https:///.well-known/maknoon/\&.json
              Works for alice@example.com handles. No DNS changes required.
  --dns       Generate a _maknoon. DNS TXT record (printed for manual setup).
  --desec     Auto-publish the DNS TXT record via deSEC.io API.
  --local     Pin identity to local contacts only (no network publishing).


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--desec\fP[=false]
	Auto-publish DNS record via deSEC.io (requires --desec-token or DESEC_TOKEN)

.PP
\fB--desec-token\fP=""
	deSEC.io API token

.PP
\fB--dns\fP[=false]
	Generate a _maknoon DNS TXT record (printed for manual setup)

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for publish

.PP
\fB--local\fP[=false]
	Pin identity to local contacts only (no network)

.PP
\fB--ttl-hours\fP=0
	Record expiry in hours (0 = config default ~48h, -1 = no expiry, e.g. 168 = 7 days)

.PP
\fB--wkd\fP[=false]
	Web Key Directory: publish as a signed HTTPS JSON file (requires alice@domain.com handle)


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--fips\fP[=false]
	Enforce strict FIPS-140 compliant cryptographic standards

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	Output results in JSON format

.PP
\fB-i\fP, \fB--name\fP="default"
	Identity name

.PP
\fB-s\fP, \fB--passphrase\fP=""
	Passphrase for the identity

.PP
\fB--passphrase-fd\fP=0
	Read passphrase from file descriptor N (e.g., --passphrase-fd 3  3<<<$(pass show key)). Also settable via MAKNOON_PASSPHRASE_FD

.PP
\fB--passphrase-file\fP=""
	Read passphrase from a file instead of prompting (use - for stdin). Also settable via MAKNOON_PASSPHRASE_FILE

.PP
